                <pb facs="0229" n="145" xml:id="pg145"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Beaupré to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-05-28"><hi rendition="#italic">May 28, 1903</hi></date>.
                        (Received 9.28 p.m., 29.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>May 28, 10 a.m. Am informed that the President has received a telegram relating
                    to large number United States employees lately arrived at Isthmus. If
                    explanation should be asked, what answer shall I make? If it is true, it will
                    intensify opposition to the ratification of the convention.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaupré.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
